  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Plateau State Emergency Response for Vulnerable Populations - Plan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The 45-day rapid response intervention (Start Fund Project 937) in the crisis-affected communities of Bassa and Bokkos LGAs of Plateau State, was activated to provide immediate lifesaving support to the affected population. The response will support the affected population to cope with the displacement, cover basic needs of the affected population including food, improve hygiene and sanitary conditions and improve the poor accommodation conditions of the displaced populations as they are currently experiencing overcrowded shelters.
This response will also address the psychological trauma experienced by the survivors, with emphasis on women and children. Key actions include but not limited to; providing counselling services, support services, and protection measures especially GBV to prevent further harm and alleviate the existing trauma while facilitating healing and recovery amongst the affected population.</narrative>
  </description>
